---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="About">
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    <div class="md:col-span-2 card space-y-4">
      <h1>About findpianoworks.com</h1>
      <section>
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          Staying current with recent publications of new music, editions, and anthologies and the
          existing body of repertoire is a time-consuming process. findpianoworks.com aims to
          centralize this large body of information in a searchable online database. In addition to
          searching for repertoire, you may search the contents of anthologies and cross-reference
          findings among multiple composers and publishers. We hope that this website will expedite
          your search process, saving you time and energy.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>History</h2>
        <p>
          The database now available through this website was originally a personal project by the
          authors that organized information on piano teaching literature. The goal was to make
          existing notes easily searchable and accessible, but the process itself proved enlightening
          and the project continued to grow. As we developed this cataloging system, we systematically
          considered the selection process teachers follow when choosing new music for their students
          and built the structure of the database accordingly. The result of these painstaking efforts
          is findpianoworks.com. Now visitors can search through a large amount of literature, sorting
          by specific criteria to find just the right piece.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>The Current Catalog</h2>
        <p>
          The current catalog includes three series of leveled anthologies: <em>Masterwork Classics</em>
          edited by Jane Magrath, the <em>Kjos Repertoire</em> series edited by Keith Snell, and the
          <em>Celebration Series</em> by Frederick Harris. These anthologies were selected since they
          include a variety of styles and techniques within the standard teaching repertoire. The catalog
          is continually growing. The authors hope to eventually include all popular anthologies and
          stay current with new releases.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="card text-sm">
        <h3>Information</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1">
          <li><a href={`${base}/about`}>About</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/methodology`}>Methodology</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/acknowledgements`}>Acknowledgements</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
